-# Zuri-Go — local workspace
+# Zuri-Go API
 
-Let’s Go to Market. Together
-
-## Open / restart
-
-Open **http://127.0.0.1:4319/?view=1&tab=overview**. Use `127.0.0.1`, because the local server checks the exact Host and Origin.
-
-If the machine has restarted, start Docker Desktop, then run:
-
-```powershell
-& D:\zuri-brand-kit\projects\zuri-go\start-local.ps1
-```
-
-PostgreSQL runs in `zuri-go-postgres` on `127.0.0.1:54329`; database `zuri_go`, persistent volume `zuri-go-postgres-data`. Node serves the app and private API on port 4319. Credentials are only in `.local/config.json` / `.local/postgres.env`, outside the published site. Do not copy these files to Vercel or the static output.
-
-## First use
-
-1. Open Overview and select **ตรวจข้อมูลเดิม**. Review campaign, task, member and meeting counts; select transcript inclusion if needed. **ยืนยันนำเข้าชุดนี้** performs one atomic import into the empty local Business. Existing browser records remain untouched. Imported lifecycle is **รอยืนยัน** until set by the user. Imports into an occupied Business are refused rather than merged automatically.
-2. Alternatively select **เริ่ม workspace ว่าง**. Meeting/Tasks/Members and campaign details then use PostgreSQL. This does not erase browser data.
-3. Register members in Meeting & Task Manager. Members are local names/profiles, not login accounts; assigning a task sends no messages.
-4. Add channel accounts from Content or Goals. Create campaigns, select channels, and confirm whether each is draft/queued/active.
-5. Plan content by month, approve it, then add one publication per channel/time. The calendar is a plan; it does not publish to social media. Mark a post published with its actual time and URL or evidence note.
-6. Set a weekly/monthly goal and select its exact accounts. For net followers, enter the cumulative baseline at Monday 00:00 / month-start 00:00 and the latest cumulative observation. Example: 1,320 minus 1,000 = **320 / 500**. Missing baseline is unknown; zero is only shown when supported by observations.
-
-All dates in the initial forms are Bangkok time. Goals may retain negative actual progress. A correction records a new observation revision with its reason; it does not erase history. Editing an approved content item invalidates its approval and scheduled publications until reviewed again.
-
-## Summary and AI
-
-The default summary is clearly marked **สรุปจากกติกา** and uses current recorded facts. An optional local Ollama adapter exists; it was not enabled or exercised against an actual model in this delivery. Set `ZURI_GO_AI_URL` to a loopback Ollama origin and `ZURI_GO_AI_MODEL` explicitly before starting the server to opt in. No cloud provider fallback, redirects or AI tools are enabled. A model may prioritize known fact IDs only; unsupported output falls back to the rule summary. Evidence snapshots are stored with each brief.
-
-## Backup
-
-The UI **Backup แคมเปญและงาน** is the compatible v2 export of those domains only. It excludes the new Business content/goals/observations. Full PostgreSQL backup:
-
-```powershell
-cd D:\zuri-brand-kit\projects\zuri-go
-node backup-local.mjs
-```
-
-This saves a private timestamped SQL dump under `.local/backups/`, including every table and isolated QA Businesses. Treat backups as private. Copy a chosen backup to your own secure backup location. Restore must target a reviewed empty database; the UI does not overwrite an existing PostgreSQL workspace. Automated scheduled backup and a full database recovery drill are outside this delivery.
-
-## Develop / verify
-
-```powershell
-node migrate.mjs
-node --test test/*.test.mjs
-```
-
-HTTP tests require the normal local server on 4319. Database tests create explicitly labeled QA Businesses, never use the configured user Business and do not delete user records. The app source is `output/draft/campaign-mission-control/src/content/`; package with the existing Data app builder and `projects/campaign-mission-control/build_unified_site.py`. Keep the protected shell and app ID unchanged.
-
-## Production — version 0.4.0
-
-The PostgreSQL site is **https://zuri-metrics-map.vercel.app/** with public Guest read-only access. Version 0.4.0 uses each Member's PID and personal password for create/edit/delete/upload actions; login opens as a modal and logout returns to Guest mode. The toolbar shows the signed-in Member name and PID. Hosted state is stored in Neon PostgreSQL, Singapore. See the release verification below for the exact promoted deployment.
-
-Chef: `ZGO-P0001`; Boss: `ZGO-P0002`; Tong: `ZGO-P0003`; K’jeab: `ZGO-P0004`. Private individual handovers are `.local/member-access/production/<PID>.json`. Share only the intended member's file; never deploy these files. PID is public and immutable, scoped to this Business; the UUID remains the PK. Historical shared/local events are not reassigned to a Member.
-
-The latest supplied backup was imported into local and cloud PostgreSQL: 1 campaign, 11 tasks, 4 members, 1 weekly plan and 45 events. Use production for shared work; local and hosted databases do not synchronize later edits. Imported campaign status needs explicit confirmation before it is counted as active or queued.
-
-Build the verified UI and unified site first, then run `python projects/zuri-go/build-cloud.py` from the workspace root. The generated `output/draft/zuri-go-cloud/` contains an allowlisted static UI and Vercel API, with private files excluded. Deploy that directory to the existing `zuri-metrics-map` project. Migration/admin credentials stay local; Vercel receives only the restricted runtime connection, Business ID, session signing secret and allowed production origin. Salted personal password hashes are stored only in the separate PostgreSQL credential table; the runtime role cannot modify that table.
-
-Migration 003 supplies persistent login rate limits. Migration 005 adds immutable PIDs, separate credentials and authenticated actor references. Member sessions validate active status, enabled credential and credential version inside the write transaction. Reset/disable and ordinary writes share Business locking; a stale concurrent transaction is rejected. Version 0.4.0 rejects the old shared password and team cookie. Existing local startup stays a trusted loopback operator workspace, without cloud synchronization or Member impersonation. Hosted import remains an operator task.
-
-Trusted operator commands from the workspace root:
-
-```powershell
-node projects/zuri-go/provision-members.mjs --cloud
-node projects/zuri-go/provision-members.mjs --cloud --reset ZGO-P0001
-node projects/zuri-go/provision-members.mjs --cloud --disable ZGO-P0001
-node projects/zuri-go/provision-members.mjs --cloud --enable ZGO-P0001
-```
-
-The first command provisions only missing credentials and verifies existing private handovers; it never silently rotates passwords. Reset generates a new private handover and invalidates previous sessions. Disable/enable also increments the credential version. A newly registered profile receives a PID automatically; only an operator enables its login. No self-service password recovery or email delivery is included. Disabling a profile blocks its sessions while inactive; use credential disable/reset to permanently revoke its existing sessions before reactivating it.
-
-See `output/draft/zuri-go-cloud-review/verification.md` for deployment identity, tests, import reconciliation, actual persistence evidence and remaining AI/FUNG/backup limitations.
-
-For version 0.4.0, see `output/draft/zuri-go/member-identity-spec.md` and `output/draft/zuri-go-member-review/verification.md` for identity architecture, migration, live checks and version diff.
-
-## Task evidence files — 0.3.1
-Open a saved task in Meeting & Task Manager, then use **แนบไฟล์ / รูปภาพ**. Up to 5 active files per task, at most 2 MiB each. The existing evidence text/link field remains available. Upload and removal save immediately, independently of saving task details. Guest can view task details, image previews and download files; upload/removal requires Member login in 0.4.0. For a new task, save it first and reopen its details to add files.
-
-Migration 004 stores file metadata and bytea in `task_attachments`, with a composite Business/Task FK and forced Business RLS. Safe raster formats have signature-based preview MIME; other files download as octet-stream under sandbox CSP and nosniff. Deleted files are soft-deleted and no longer downloadable. Full database backups include bytes; **v2 JSON Backup does not include attachments**. Local and hosted files do not synchronize.
-
-Specification: `output/draft/zuri-go/guest-access-spec.md`. Verification and version diff: `output/draft/zuri-go-guest-review/`.
+Active service source, migrations and backend tests. See [project README](../../README.md) and [operations runbook](../../docs/operations/runbook.md) for current commands. Local private configuration is ../../.local, resolved relative to modules rather than shell cwd.
